{
  "_README": "Weights + specs transcribed from Decathlon in-store comparison spec boards (photographed by user, batch 1 = 13 photos, 2026-07-07). Decathlon supplies NO weights via Awin and 403s all scraping, so these store boards are the weight source. KEY = Decathlon 8-digit article/model code (joins to the Awin feed's model/product code). `skus` lists every code shown for that model (color/size variants share a model but may differ by code). weightGrams = the board's stated weight; for size-variant products (pads L/XL, bags 'in size L') see weightBySize + weightRefNote. Third-party brands sold at Decathlon (Petzl/Black Diamond/Komperdell/Deuter/Sea to Summit) are marked thirdParty:true — capture the weight but the Decathlon/Awin offer is a RESOLD offer (brand != retailer), same pattern as the FF-resold Arc/Pat items. NO-WEIGHT items (lanterns, flashlights, Arpenaz daypacks, car-camping air beds) are listed under _noWeightAvailable for scope reference only.",
  "_batch": 2,
  "_photoBatchesExpected": "user will make one more store trip to fill gaps (see _gapsToPhotograph)",
  "_joinMechanics": {
    "feed": "AWIN advertiser feed fid/65881 (.env AWIN_DECATHLON_FEED_URL), UK/English, ~57.6k rows. Download: curl -sL $URL | gunzip. NOT the 5,368-row category feed (that one is mostly apparel; tents/bags/pads/headlamps absent).",
    "joinKey": "The 8-digit store article code = the PREFIX of `merchant_product_id` (e.g. '8858233-5133809' -> '8858233'). NOT `model_number` (that is a different internal id like '310893'). Join store-specs skus[] to feed rows via merchant_product_id.split('-')[0].",
    "multiRow": "One article code appears in MULTIPLE feed rows — one per merchant_category it's merchandised in. Collect all rows for a code; pick the most descriptive merchant_category (drop promo buckets: Summer Sale, Womens Sale, Hiking Sale, New Collection, Sportswear Accessories, Festival Bags). parent_product_id is EMPTY (no variant grouping from feed).",
    "offer": "aw_deep_link is the awin1.com pclick affiliate URL -> use as MerchantOffer.deepLink (network 'awin', merchantId 26895, merchantName 'Decathlon'). Image from merchant_image_url / aw_image_url (+ alternate_image*). Price from search_price. Filter in_stock=1.",
    "brandAuthority": "Use the feed's brand_name, NOT the brand guessed in this file. The MT500/MT900 trekking TENTS and PACKS come through as brand=SIMOND in the feed (Decathlon shifted the MT trekking line to Simond). Reconcile at build time.",
    "attributeSource": "For PHOTOGRAPHED items use the specs in THIS file (capacity/comfortTempC/rValue/capacityLiters/fill etc.) — richer + exact. merchant_category parsing is only a fallback for non-photographed breadth items (encodes capacity '3 Man Tents', volume '20L to 30L Backpacks', etc.)."
  },
